REFERENCE           HERO_DESCRIPTION
LANG_ENGLISH        "A marksman and skirmisher class specializing in long-range combat while offering close range options to surprise your opponents. It relies on agility for survivability.\n> Weapons\n- Pistol\nWth low firerate, high damage and full accuracy the pistol is a high skill ceiling option capable of quickly dispatching enemies.\n-- Level 1: A standard pistol.\n-- Level 2: Unlocks an alternate charged fire mode.\n-- Level 3: Grants a high-powered primary fire and charge mode with increased ammo consumption. Toggle weapon mode to revert to the standard pistol, the alt. fire in this mode fires a triple-shot burst-fire\n- E-11 Blaster\nA highly versatile blaster rifle with two distinct firing modes: a slow, hard-hitting primary fire with superior projectile velocity, increases the clip capacity as well as reload rate.\n-- Level 1: A standard blaster rifle with slow primary fire and high velocity.\n-- Level 2: Adds a faster firing alt. fire.\n-- Level 3: Makes alt. fire accurate when walking and standing still, and increases the clip capacity.\n- Projectile Rifle\nA dedicated sniper weapon that cannot be upgraded. Features two zoom levels switched with weapon mode. Must always be fired while scoped, jumping while scoped is not possible, and the rifle is only accurate when standing completely still.\n \n> Abilities & Utility\n- Frag Grenade\nA basic explosive grenade. Pressing and holding the primary fire key, while the grenade is selected will result in the grenade being charged. The longer the frag grenade is charged, the greater the throwing range capability becomes.\nAlternate fire of the grenade can be primed and with good timing made to explode right at the feet of the enemy, knocking them down instantly, the blast radius and damage done is vastly reduced in comparison to primary mode. Hitting an enemy directly will also detonate the grenade. Charging the alternate fire further extends the throwing range.\nSwitch to another weapon at any time to cancel a charge.\n-- Level 1: One Frag Grenade.\n-- Level 2: Additional Frag Grenade.\n-- Level 3: Additional Frag Grenade.\n \n \n- Dodge [Class Special 1]\nThe Hero can dodge incoming blaster fire by expending dodge points. The closer the attacker, the more points are consumed per shot. Dodging is unavailable at very close range. Cannot dodge attacks from the back, at very close range, while electorcuted, or poisoned.\n-- Level 1: Grants the ability to dodge.\n-- Level 2: Decreases passive dodge points drain while the ability is active.\n-- Level 3: Further decreases passive dodge points drain while the ability is active, the minimum distance required for dodge is now shorter.\n- Dash [Class Special 2]\nHero dashes in the direction if their movement, covering a small distance. Combined with outstanding movement speed, Dash enables rapid repositioning to key map locations, quick retreats to cover, or last-second escapes from a charging Sith.\n-- Level 1: Unlocks the ability.\n-- Level 2: The cooldown of the ability is now lower.\n- Heal\nThe Hero passively regenerates health over time up to certain breakpoints, determined by the ability level.\n-- Level 1: Slow healing with the breakpoints every 25hp.\n-- Level 2: Slightly faster with breakpoints every 30hp.\n-- Level 3: Fast healing with the breakpoints every 35hp.\n- Quick Throw [Class Special 3]\nAllows the Hero to instantly prime and release any grenade without switching to it first, keeping weapons ready while staying on the offensive.\n-- Level 1: Throw Frag Grenades (primary fire) with CS3.\n-- Level 2: Throw Frag Grenades (secondary fire) with CS3, or primary fire with Use + CS3.\n-- Level 3: Quickthrow can be activated while rolling."

