REFERENCE           CLASSINFO_SOLDIER
LANG_ENGLISH        "^4SOLDIER^7\nThe Soldier class represents the common soldier, as such, Soldiers have the most lives but trade it for less health, armor and mobility.\n^2> Weaponry^7\n- \rPistol\r\nBasic pistol, always accurate with low firerate and modest damage.\n-- Level 1: A standard pistol.\n-- Level 2: Unlocks an alternate charged fire mode.\n \n- \rE-11 Blaster\r\nA highly versatile blaster rifle with two distinct firing modes: a slow, hard-hitting primary fire with superior projectile velocity, and a rapid secondary fire suited for close-quarters engagements.\n-- Level 1: A standard blaster rifle with slow primary fire and high velocity.\n-- Level 2: Adds a faster firing alt. fire.\n-- Level 3: Makes alt. fire accurate when walking and standing still, increases the clip capacity as well as reload rate.\n \n- \rE-22 Rifle\r\nA double-stacked blaster firing in a two-shot burst on primary fire. The secondary mode fires a large, high-damage projectile with significant ammo drain.\n-- Level 1: Grants the weapon with primary fire only.\n-- Level 2: Attaches a scope for long range combat, toggled with alt. fire.\n-- Level 3: Secondary mode can be toggled with weapon mode switch for fully automatic fire.\n \n^3> Abilities & Utility^7\n- \rFrag Grenade\r\nA basic explosive grenade. Pressing and holding the primary fire key, while the grenade is selected will result in the grenade being charged. The longer the frag grenade is charged, the greater the throwing range capability becomes.\nAlternate fire of the grenade can be primed and with good timing made to explode right at the feet of the enemy, knocking them down instantly, the blast radius and damage done is vastly reduced in comparison to primary mode. Hitting an enemy directly will also detonate the grenade. Charging the alternate fire further extends the throwing range.\nSwitch to another weapon at any time to cancel a charge.\n- \rConcussion Grenade\r\nConcussion Grenade can be charged much like the secondary fire of the frag grenade, and explode right at the enemy’s feet, hitting an enemy directly will also detonate the grenade. This grenade has a larger explosion radius than Frag nade’s alternate fire.\nSwitch to another weapon at any time to cancel a charge.\n- Close Combat Training\n-- Level 1: Improves movespeed when Melee is equipped (1.2x) and enables all Melee techniques. Without this perk, Soldiers are limited to basic punches\n-- Level 2: 1.2x move speed in melee, 1.1x speed with weapon drawn, can now utilize roll getups.\n-- Level 3: 1.2x move speed even with weapon equipped.\n- Reinforcements\n-- Level 1: One additional life.\n-- Level 2: Another additional life.\n- Assemble\nIf a Soldier dies with remaining reinforcements while within range of an allied Commander with the Rally perk (indicated by a green circle at their feet), they will respawn next to that unit with a temporary boost to HP and movement speed.\nWhile dead, press the USE key to ignore any Rally spawns and spawn at a regular spawn point. You will not receive the HP and movespeed boost if you do this.\n-- Level 1: Enables rally spawn.\n-- Level 2: when rally spawning, gain 1.2x bonus movement speed and 20 temp hp for 10 seconds.\n-- Level 3: when rally spawning, gain 1.2x bonus movement speed and 30 temp hp for 20 seconds.\n"

REFERENCE           CLASSINFO_TROOPER
LANG_ENGLISH        "^1SOLDIER^7\nThe Soldier class represents the common soldier, as such, Soldiers have the most lives but trade it for less health, armor and mobility.\n^2> Weaponry\n- \rPistol\r\nBasic pistol, always accurate with low firerate and modest damage.\n-- Level 1: A standard pistol.\n-- Level 2: Unlocks an alternate charged fire mode.\n- \rE-11 Blaster\r\nA highly versatile blaster rifle with two distinct firing modes: a slow, hard-hitting primary fire with superior projectile velocity, and a rapid secondary fire suited for close-quarters engagements.\n-- Level 1: A standard blaster rifle with slow primary fire and high velocity.\n-- Level 2: Adds a faster firing alt. fire.\n-- Level 3: Makes alt. fire accurate when walking and standing still, increases the clip capacity as well as reload rate.\n \n- \rCR-2 Repeating Pistol\r\nA fast-firing weapon built for close-range encounters. Its compact size causes accuracy bloom when shooting for extended periods of time, so controlled short bursts are essential for staying on target.\n-- Level 1: Grants the weapon.\n-- Level 2: Increases clip size.\n-- Level 3: Increases rate of fire.\n \n^3> Abilities & Utility^7\n- \rFrag Grenade\r\nA basic explosive grenade. Pressing and holding the primary fire key, while the grenade is selected will result in the grenade being charged. The longer the frag grenade is charged, the greater the throwing range capability becomes.\nAlternate fire of the grenade can be primed and with good timing made to explode right at the feet of the enemy, knocking them down instantly, the blast radius and damage done is vastly reduced in comparison to primary mode. Hitting an enemy directly will also detonate the grenade. Charging the alternate fire further extends the throwing range.\nSwitch to another weapon at any time to cancel a charge.\n- \rConcussion Grenade\r\nA concussion Grenade can be charged much like the secondary fire of the frag grenade, and explode right at the enemy’s feet, hitting an enemy directly will also detonate the grenade. This grenade has a larger explosion radius than Frag nade’s alternate fire.\nSwitch to another weapon at any time to cancel a charge.\n- Close Combat Training\n-- Level 1: Improves movespeed when Melee is equipped (1.2x) and enables all Melee techniques. Without this perk, Soldiers are limited to basic punches\n-- Level 2: 1.2x move speed in melee, 1.1x speed with weapon drawn, can now utilize roll getups.\n-- Level 3: 1.2x move speed even with a weapon equipped.\n- Reinforcements\n-- Level 1: One additional life.\n-- Level 2: Another additional life.\n- Assemble\nIf a Soldier dies with remaining reinforcements while within range of an allied Commander with the Rally perk (indicated by a green circle at their feet), they will respawn next to that unit with a temporary boost to HP and movement speed.\nWhile dead, press the USE key to ignore any Rally spawns and spawn at a regular spawn point. You will not receive the HP and movespeed boost if you do this.\n-- Level 1: Enables rally spawn.\n-- Level 2: when rally spawning, gain 1.2x bonus movement speed and 20 temp hp for 10 seconds.\n-- Level 3: when rally spawning, gain 1.2x bonus movement speed and 30 temp hp for 20 seconds.\n"

REFERENCE           CLASSINFO_ET
LANG_ENGLISH        "^1ELITE TROOPER^7\nAs elite infantry, Elite Troopers have fewer lives than Soldiers, but more health, speed, and customization options. They can be configured as Soldier spawn points, heavy blaster specialists, or grenadiers.\n^2> Weaponry\n- \rPistol\r\nBasic pistol, always accurate with low firerate and modest damage.\n-- Level 1: A standard pistol.\n-- Level 2: Unlocks an alternate charged fire mode.\n- \rE-11 Blaster\r\nA highly versatile blaster rifle with two distinct firing modes: a slow, hard-hitting primary fire with superior projectile velocity, and a rapid secondary fire suited for close-quarters engagements.\n-- Level 1: A standard blaster rifle with slow primary fire and high velocity.\n-- Level 2: Adds a faster firing alt. fire.\n-- Level 3: Makes alt. fire accurate when walking and standing still, increases the clip capacity as well as reload rate.\n- \rA280\r\nA long range carbine with high velocity and low fire rate, which can also utilize burst mode for devastating effect at close range.\n-- Level 1: A basic shot that deals high damage for low ammo cost. Never accurate unless standing or crouching still.\n-- Level 2: Adds a burst fire mode on secondary weapon mode. Primary mode is now also accurate when walking.\n-- Level 3: Adds a scope.\n^3> Abilities & Utility^7\n- \rFrag Grenade\r\nA basic explosive grenade. Pressing and holding the primary fire key, while the grenade is selected will result in the grenade being charged. The longer the frag grenade is charged, the greater the throwing range capability becomes.\nAlternate fire of the grenade can be primed and with good timing made to explode right at the feet of the enemy, knocking them down instantly, the blast radius and damage done is vastly reduced in comparison to primary mode. Hitting an enemy directly will also detonate the grenade. Charging the alternate fire further extends the throwing range.\nSwitch to another weapon at any time to cancel a charge.\n-- Level 1: One Frag Grenade.\n-- Level 2: Additional Frag Grenade.\n- \rSonic Grenade\r\nA stun grenade that prevents affected players from attacking or jumping while reducing their movement speed. Pressing and holding the primary fire key, while the grenade is selected, will result in the grenade being charged. The longer the frag grenade is charged, the greater the throwing range capability becomes.\nSecondary fire will place the grenade as a mine, which will trigger when an enemy comes nearby.\nSBD and Droideka cannot be affected by sonic grenade.\n-- Level 1: Grants one Sonic Grenade.\n-- Level 2: Another Sonic Grenade.\n- Reinforcement\n-- Level 1: Get one additional life.\n- Rally\nThe Elite becomes a walking spawn point for allied Soldiers. Soldiers who rally to them receive a bonus 20 HP and increased movement speed.\n-- Level 1: You become a walking spawn point for Soldiers.\n- Dodge ^3[Class Special 1]^7\nThe Elite can dodge incoming blaster fire by expending dodge points. The closer the attacker, the more points are consumed per shot. Dodging is unavailable at very close range. Cannot dodge attacks from the back, at very close range, while electrocuted, or poisoned.\n-- Level 1: Grants the ability to dodge.\n-- Level 2: Decreases passive dodge points drain while the ability is active.\n"

REFERENCE           CLASSINFO_COMMANDER
LANG_ENGLISH        "^4Commander^7\nAs elite infantry, Commanders have fewer lives than Soldiers, but more health, speed, and customization options. They can be configured as Soldier spawn points, heavy blaster specialists, and grenadiers.\n^2> Weaponry^7\nBasic pistol, always accurate with low firerate and modest damage.\n-- Level 1: A standard pistol.\n-- Level 2: Unlocks an alternate charged fire mode.\n- E-11 Blaster\nA highly versatile blaster rifle with two distinct firing modes: a slow, hard-hitting primary fire with superior projectile velocity, and a rapid secondary fire suited for close-quarters engagements.\n-- Level 1: A standard blaster rifle with slow primary fire and high velocity.\n-- Level 2: Adds a faster firing alt. fire.\n-- Level 3: Makes alt. fire accurate when walking and standing still, increases the clip capacity as well as reload rate.\n- T-21\nA high powered rifle with very slow firing primary fire featuring massive damage, and a more standard secondary fire.\n-- Level 1: A powerful shot that deals massive damage for high ammo cost and causes knock-back on its user. Shooting mid air will knock the user down.\n-- Level 2: Unlocks alrt fire, hold down to rapidly fire your carbine at your enemies but this fire mode is only accurate while standing still.\n-- Level 3: Increases primary fire firerate and the clip size of the gun.\n^3> Abilities & Utility^7\n- Frag Grenade\nA basic explosive grenade. Pressing and holding the primary fire key, while the grenade is selected will result in the grenade being charged. The longer the frag grenade is charged, the greater the throwing range capability becomes.\nAlternate fire of the grenade can be primed and with good timing made to explode right at the feet of the enemy, knocking them down instantly, the blast radius and damage done is vastly reduced in comparison to primary mode. Hitting an enemy directly will also detonate the grenade. Charging of the secondary fire function will allow for greater throwing range.\nYou can cancel charging a grenade by switching to a different weapon.\n-- Level 1: One Frag Grenade.\n-- Level 2: Additional Frag Grenade.\n \n- Fire Grenade\nTapping primary fire will result in a short toss of the grenade. Pressing and holding primary fire will allow for the grenade's throwing distance to increase (the longer you \"charge\" the longer the toss).\nSecondary fire will cause the grenade to explode on impact with a surface, this has a smaller area of effect.\nThe explosion of the Fire Grenade depends on where it detonates. If it detonates on the ground, a large circle of fire is created. If it detonates in the air, multiple small clumps of fire are spread around the vicinity.\nThe fire will slow down a player moving through it, causing afterburn which must be put out via rolling.\n-- Level 1: Grants one Fire Grenade.\n-- Level 2: Another Fire Grenade.\n- Reinforcement\n-- Level 1: Get one additional life.\n- Rally\nThe Commander becomes a walking spawn point for allied Soldiers. Soldiers who rally to them receive a bonus 20 HP and increased movement speed.\n-- Level 1: You become a walking spawn point for Soldiers.\n- Dodge ^3[Class Special 1]^7\nThe Commander can dodge incoming blaster fire by expending dodge points. The closer the attacker, the more points are consumed per shot. Dodging is unavailable at very close range. Cannot dodge attacks from the back, at very close range, while electrocuted, or poisoned.\n-- Level 1: Grants the ability to dodge.\n-- Level 2: Decreases passive dodge points drain while the ability is active.\n"

REFERENCE           CLASSINFO_JEDI
LANG_ENGLISH        "TODO"

REFERENCE           CLASSINFO_SITH
LANG_ENGLISH        "^4SITH^7\nThe Sith is the most versatile class on the blue team, being able to act as skirmisher, frontliner, pusher and support for their team. They can deflect blaster fire with their lightsaber, move around with ease by utilizing Force Jump and Force Speed. However, due to lack of armor a well placed shot can be devastating.\n^5> Force Powers^7\n- \rJump\r\nForce Jump enables the user to leap great heights with the help of the Force.\n-- Level 1: The user can jump higher than a normal person, and can perform acrobatics like backflips and special moves with a lightsaber (Left/Right + Jump + Attack).\n-- Level 2: The user can jump higher than level 1. Force Points drain is also reduced. Enables wall run and wall flip (Move towards a wall and jump).\n-- Level 3: Jump height is further increased and Force Point drain is reduced. Wallruns also drain less Force Points. Enables Wall Grab when facing or facing away from a wall and holding jump mid air.\n- \rPush\r\nForce Push enables the user to shove away people, projectiles and world objects from a distance with the Force.\n-- Level 1: Pushes back rockets, grenades, and other projectiles. Shoves a player back a small distance.\n-- Level 2: Can now knock down a single player if they are running or jumping by aiming at them. It also pushes rockets and grenades back in the direction you aim.\n-- Level 3: Can knock down all opponents in the area of effect if they’re running or jumping and no longer requires crosshair aim.\n- \rPull\r\nWith Force Pull, the user can steal other player's guns and knock them over.\n-- Level 1: Pulls a player towards you a short distance, can also be used to pull rockets and grenades in a direction.\n-- Level 2: Can now knock down a single player if they are running or jumping by aiming at them.\n-- Level 3: Can stagger all running or jumping opponents in the area of effect and will pull down and steal the weapon of an enemy when aimed at.\n\n- Super Push\nRequires Pull and Push level 3. Pull your target first, then push them to launch them with tremendous force. Deals massive damage if they collide with an obstacle.\n- Repulse ^3[Class Special 1 in Melee]^7\nSends out a powerful wave of force which knocks down and away all running enemies around you, dealing massive damage if they hit an obstacle. Requires Push 3, Pull 3 and no Blaster/Saber Defense.\n\n- Seeing\nAllows the user to sense other players through walls.\n-- Level 1: Shows enemies on radar.\n-- Level 2: Shows enemies on radar, highlights nearby friendly players and NPCs while active, and can see them through walls. Enemies can be seen when they attack. Extended range compared to level 1, FP cost is reduced.\n-- Level 3: Displays enemies on radar. Highlights all nearby players and NPCs, color-coded by allegiance. Lower FP cost and greater range than Level 2. No activation sound after initial use. While active, you can dodge Sniper and Disruptor body shots and see the health and armor of the player in your crosshair.\n- Lightning\nForce Lightning deals damage to enemies, reduces their rate of fire and finally stuns them.\n-- Level 1: The Sith casts a line of lightning in front of them dealing damage and reducing the fire rate of an enemy’s blaster fire.\n-- Level 2: The arc of lightning is now larger and the forcepower can be used until your Forcepool runs out.\n-- Level 3: Lightning now pierces enemies. Can be channelled with two hands if Melee is equipped in order to increase damage done. Two handed lightning can be combined with Push 3 to perform a Lightning Push, knocking down running opponents for a longer time and even further increasing damage done by lightning\n- Grip\nGrip is used to choke enemies. At higher levels it can be used to lift enemies from the ground and move them around at your will.\nIn order to use grip, you must target an enemy and hold the grip button for a certain period of time. During this time a small red 'gripping' hand will appear on your target. Being shot while attempting to grip delays the progress. Grip can be countered with Force Push, Force Pull, or Force Mind Trick.\n-- Level 1: Grants Force Grip, enemies can still move around and attack while gripped.\n-- Level 2: Reduces Force Points drain and increases damage. Gripped enemies will now be lifted up and cannot move or attack.\n-- Level 3: Further reduces Force Points drain and increases damage. Gripped enemies will now be lifted up and can be moved around by the user.\n> Lightsaber\nThe Lightsaber is the only weapon and main offensive and defensive tool of the Sith, being able to deflect blaster fire and block lightsaber attacks, but also kill enemies even in one strike.\n- Saber Styles\nThe Lightsaber features different fighting styles which differ in speed, defense and damage done. Fast Styles are the fastest while offering low damage, Medium styles strive for balance, and heavy styles try to overwhelm their enemies with high damage but sacrifice speed and defense. Please consult the library and/or the wiki for in-depth explanation of each style.\n-- Fast Styles\n--- Level 1: Grants Blue Lightsaber style.\n--- Level 2: Grants Cyan Lightsaber style.\n--- Level 3: Grants Blue and Cyan Lightsaber styles.\n-- Medium Styles\n--- Level 1: Grants Yellow Lightsaber style.\n--- Level 2: Grants Dual or Staff Lightsaber style (selectable in the hilt menu).\n--- Level 3: Grants Yellow and Dual or Staff Lightsaber styles.\n-- Heavy Styles\n--- Level 1: Grants Red Lightsaber style.\n--- Level 2: Grants Purple Lightsaber style.\n--- Level 3: Grants Red and Purple Lightsaber styles.\n- Saber Throw\n-- Level 0: Vertical Saber throw which travels in an arc.\n-- Level 1: Grants Horizontal saber throw which travels in a straight line.\n-- Level 2: Allows the player to guide the thrown saber toward their crosshair and increases range.\n-- Level 3: Further increases throw range.\n- Saber Defense\nSaber Defense determines the ability of the saber user to block incoming lightsaber attacks using block points.\n--- Level 1: Decreases the damage taken from lightsaber attacks and activates Block Points regeneration.\n--- Level 2: Further decreases the damage taken from lightsaber attacks and increases Block Points regeneration.\n--- Level 3: Extends the blocking arc to better block attacks from the sides. Killing enemies will now regen a portion of BP. BP cost of Special Attacks is now halved.\n-- Blaster Defense\nBlaster Defense determines the ability of the saber user to block incoming blaster fire using block points. BD level cannot be higher than the level of Saber Defense.\n--- Level 1: Decreases the FP damage taken from blaster fire.\n--- Level 2: Further decreases the FP damage taken from blaster fire.\n--- Level 3: Even further decreases the FP damage taken from blaster fire. Removes fp penalty on airborne shots.\n \n-- Blaster Deflect\nGrants ability to deflect blaster fire back to a point designated by the user’s crosshari holding Alt. Fire + Fire (Block and Attack) at the same time, also reduces FP damage taken while swingblocking. Timing the deflect while blocking will further reduce FP damage from blasters.\n--- Level 1: Grants the ability to deflect blaster fire back at enemies.\n--- Level 2: Reduces Deflect force points drain, FP drained by blaster fire, and increases the Timed Deflect window.\n--- Level 3: Further reduces Deflect force points drain, FP drained by blaster fire, and further increases the Timed Deflect window.\n \n^3> Abilities^7\n- Force Block\nProtects against the usage of Force Powers. An enemy force user can use force focus by aiming at the force block user to bypass force block.\n-- Level 1: Immunity against force powers while above 90 FP.\n-- Level 2: Immunity against force powers while above 70 FP.\n-- Level 3: Immunity against force powers while above 50 FP.\n"

REFERENCE           CLASSINFO_HERO
LANG_ENGLISH        "^1HERO^7\nA marksman and skirmisher class specializing in long-range combat while offering close range options to surprise your opponents. It relies on agility for survivability.\n^2> Weaponry\n- \rPistol\r\nWth low firerate, high damage and full accuracy the pistol is a high skill ceiling option capable of quickly dispatching enemies.\n-- Level 1: A standard pistol.\n-- Level 2: Unlocks an alternate charged fire mode.\n-- Level 3: Grants a high-powered primary fire and charge mode with increased ammo consumption. Toggle weapon mode to revert to the standard pistol, the alt. fire in this mode fires a triple-shot burst-fire\n- \rE-11 Blaster\r\nA highly versatile blaster rifle with two distinct firing modes: a slow, hard-hitting primary fire with superior projectile velocity, increases the clip capacity as well as reload rate.\n-- Level 1: A standard blaster rifle with slow primary fire and high velocity.\n-- Level 2: Adds a faster firing alt. fire.\n-- Level 3: Makes alt. fire accurate when walking and standing still, and increases the clip capacity.\n- Projectile Rifle\nA dedicated sniper weapon that cannot be upgraded. Features two zoom levels switched with weapon mode. Must always be fired while scoped, jumping while scoped is not possible, and the rifle is only accurate when standing completely still.\n \n^3> Abilities & Utility^7\n- \rFrag Grenade\r\nA basic explosive grenade. Pressing and holding the primary fire key, while the grenade is selected will result in the grenade being charged. The longer the frag grenade is charged, the greater the throwing range capability becomes.\nAlternate fire of the grenade can be primed and with good timing made to explode right at the feet of the enemy, knocking them down instantly, the blast radius and damage done is vastly reduced in comparison to primary mode. Hitting an enemy directly will also detonate the grenade. Charging the alternate fire further extends the throwing range.\nSwitch to another weapon at any time to cancel a charge.\n-- Level 1: One Frag Grenade.\n-- Level 2: Additional Frag Grenade.\n-- Level 3: Additional Frag Grenade.\n \n- Dodge ^3[Class Special 1]^7\nThe Hero can dodge incoming blaster fire by expending dodge points. The closer the attacker, the more points are consumed per shot. Dodging is unavailable at very close range. Cannot dodge attacks from the back, at very close range, while electrocuted, or poisoned.\n-- Level 1: Grants the ability to dodge.\n-- Level 2: Decreases passive dodge points drain while the ability is active.\n-- Level 3: Further decreases passive dodge points drain while the ability is active, the minimum distance required for dodge is now shorter.\n- Dash ^3[Class Special 2]^7\nHero dashes in the direction if their movement, covering a small distance. Combined with outstanding movement speed, Dash enables rapid repositioning to key map locations, quick retreats to cover, or last-second escapes from a charging Sith.\n-- Level 1: Unlocks the ability.\n-- Level 2: The cooldown of the ability is now lower.\n- Heal\nThe Hero passively regenerates health over time up to certain breakpoints, determined by the ability level.\n-- Level 1: Slow healing with the breakpoints every 25hp.\n-- Level 2: Slightly faster with breakpoints every 30hp.\n-- Level 3: Fast healing with the breakpoints every 35hp.\n- Quick Throw ^3[Class Special 3]^7\nAllows the Hero to instantly prime and release any grenade without switching to it first, keeping weapons ready while staying on the offensive.\n-- Level 1: Throw Frag Grenades (primary fire) with CS3.\n-- Level 2: Throw Frag Grenades (secondary fire) with CS3, or primary fire with Use + CS3.\n-- Level 3: Quickthrow can be activated while rolling.\n"

REFERENCE           CLASSINFO_MANDALORIAN
LANG_ENGLISH        "^4MANDALORIAN^7\nThe Mandalorian is a very versatile class, capable of serving as a skirmisher thanks to their jetpack, brawler and tank thanks to the beskar armor, sniper with the ee-4 or Amban Rifle, or Jedi hunter, by utilizing the many gadgets at their disposal.\n^2> Weaponry\n- \rWestar Pistol\r\nA standard sidearm that is always accurate, with low fire rate and modest damage. Its potential grows substantially when dual wielded.\n-- Level 1: A standard pistol.\n-- Level 2: Enables alt. fire charged shot - higher charge increases the damage.\n-- Level 3: Enables dual wield, double the fire power.\n- \rEE-3 Carbine\r\nA highly accurate burst-fire weapon capable of dealing consistent and significant damage. Engaging the scope switches to full-auto fire, though it cannot be used while running.\n-- Level 1: Grants the weapon, fires in a 3-shot burst\n-- Level 2: The gun's rate of fire is faster, and a scope is granted. Aiming down scope enables full-auto fire.\n-- Level 3: Further decreases time between shots and time between bursts. Additionally, the gun is now always accurate.\n- \rEE-4 Carbine\r\nA high-damage carbine with accuracy that degrades under sustained fire, short bursts and quick engagements are strongly recommended. A dedicated sniper mode when scoped delivers powerful, fast-moving shots at the cost of higher ammo consumption.\n-- Level 1: Issues the basic EE-4 Carbine with primary fire only.\n-- Level 2: The gun's rate of fire is faster, and a scope is granted. Accuracy also degrades slightly more slowly.\n-- Level 3: Unlocks sniper mode (toggle with weapon mode key). Sniper shots must be fired while scoped, deal increased damage, and travel significantly faster, but drain more ammo.\n- \rAmban Rifle\r\nA mobile sniper rifle that blends the traits of the Disruptor Rifle and Projectile Rifle. It lacks the Projectile Rifle's firing delay, and uses Disruptor-style charge-up. While damage is lower than the Projectile Rifle, the Amban offers more ammo and a higher fire rate. Scoping is required to charge a shot. Unscoped primary fire serves as a stun baton - dealing low damage, knocking enemies back, and briefly preventing them from attacking.\n-- Level 1: Issues the Amban Rifle with snipe mode only.\n-- Level 2: Adds ability to stun on unscoped primary fire.\n \n^3> Abilities & Utility^7\n- Beskar Armor\nA layered defensive system that mitigates damage from blasters, explosives, and even lightsabers. Equipping Beskar Armor removes the ability to perform a side-roll getup.\n-- Level 1: Reduces damage from lightsabers and explosives, and damage dealt by blaster fire to the torso.\n-- Level 2: Now also provides protection from blaster fire to the head.\n-- Level 3: Covers limbs and further reduces overall damage taken.\n- Fuel\nRequired for use of the Mandalorian jetpack and flamethrower.\n-- Level 1: Provides the player with some fuel and enables Jetpack. You can go airborne with your Jetpack when you have enough fuel by holding JUMP key or double tapping it. Disabling the Jetpack is done with USE key.\n-- Level 2: Further tops up the fuel tank.\n-- Level 3: Increases the fuel to the maximum level.\n- Flamethrower ^3[Class Special 2]^7\nProjects a stream of fire that cannot be blocked by Jedi. Does not affect enemies at point-blank range and consumes fuel. Use the Weapon Mode switch in melee to alternate between the Flamethrower and the Wrist Laser.\n-- Level 1: Equips the wrist-mounted flamethrower.\n- Rocket ^3[Class Special 1]^7\nA single-use jetpack-mounted rocket that deals massive damage on impact. Cannot be equipped simultaneously with Whistling Birds.\n-- Level 1: Equips one jetpack rocket.\n- Whistling Birds ^3[Class Special 1]^7\nHold Class Special 1 and aim at targets to lock on and maintain the hold until lock-on completes. Releasing CS1 launches one rocket per locked target. Partial lock-ons are possible but result in more erratic missile trajectories and possible misses. Hold USE to cancel all current targets. Cannot be equipped simultaneously with the Jetpack Rocket.\n- Wrist Laser ^3[Class Special 2]^7\nA slow firing laser with high velocity which deals massive damage to enemies or a Jedi’s force points. Holds up to 4 shots, which regenerate slowly over time. Rapidly firing all 4 shots will trigger a malfunction cooldown before regeneration resumes.\n"

REFERENCE           CLASSINFO_SBD
LANG_ENGLISH        "^4SUPER BATTLE DROID^7\nSBDs are ultra-heavy gunners offering exceptional firepower and durability, at the cost of slow movement and the inability to jump or move while crouching. Managing their battery is essential for maintaining peak combat efficiency\n^2> Weaponry^7\nThe SBD only features a built-in Arm Blaster which can be upgraded with various abilities. Class Special 2 performs a powerful slap that knocks down any non-crouching, non-Wookiee opponent.\n^3> Abilities & Utility^7\n- Hull Strength\nIncreases the SBD's total health pool.\n-- Level 1: Increased amount of health.\n-- Level 2: Even more health.\n-- Level 3: Maximum amount of health.\n - Firepower\nIncreases the firing rate of the built-in Arm Blaster.\n-- Level 1: Faster fire rate.\n-- Level 2: Even faster fire rate.\n-- Level 3: Maximum firepower.\n- Recharge Boost\nReduces battery drain from various actions and increases regeneration rate. ^3Class Special 1^7 toggles Low Power Mode - the Arm Blaster is deactivated and movement is restricted to walking, but battery regenerates at an accelerated rate and any active fire is extinguished.\nIn Low Power Mode, hold ^3Class Special 2^7 to convert Arm Blaster ammo into battery charge.\n-- Level 1: Recharge rate is increased, can recharge while walking. Battery is lost when running, or firing while walking.\n-- Level 2: Recharge rate is increased further. Battery is constant when running, or firing while walking.\n-- Level 3: Recharge rate is maximized. Battery charges unless running and firing simultaneously.\n- Advanced Logic\nProvides resistance against Jedi Mind Trick.\n-- Level 1: The SBD is able to see mind-tricking jedi flickering with a blue aura for a short period every 3 seconds.\n-- Level 2: The Jedi flickers once a second.\n- Advanced Targeting\nAllows the SBD to zoom their view using class special 2. Blaster shots now originate at the center of your screen.\n-- Level 1: Enables the scope.\n- Advanced Radar\nShows enemies on the radar when the SBD is in low power mode.\n-- Level 1: Enables the radar.\n- Cortosis\n-- Level 1: Provides significant protection against a lightsaber's cutting power\n-- Level 2: Causes a short stagger when a lightsaber attack contacts the SBD.\n- Blast Armour\n-- Level 1: Provides significant protection against explosions, shrapnel, melee attacks, and the projectile rifle.\n- Magnetic Plating\n-- Level 1: Provides significant protection against blaster weaponry, including deflecting blaster bolts from the SBD.\n"

REFERENCE           CLASSINFO_CLONE
LANG_ENGLISH        "^1CLONE TROOPER^7\nThe Clone Trooper is a versatile frontline unit adaptable to the team's needs. They can field a secondary life and have access to powerful weaponry, making them a dependable and well-rounded combatant.\n^2> Weaponry^7\n- \rClone Pistol\r\nThe primary fire on the clone pistol shoots a basic bolt. Holding secondary fire charges a shot that bounces off walls.\n-- Level 1: A standard-issue pistol, with nothing special about it.\n-- Level 2: Enables secondary charged bouncing shot - higher charge allows for more bounces.\n- \rClonetrooper Rifle\r\nThe Clonetrooper Rifle is a fast firing repeating rifle used by Clone Troopers that can be fitted with an energy blast launcher, commonly known as \"blobs\", these blasts are a special purchasable ability for Clone Troopers armed with the Clonetrooper Rifle.\n-- Level 1: Clone Rifle with low rate of fire.\n-- Level 2: Improved rate of fire.\n-- Level 3: The Clonetrooper Rifle has an extremely rapid rate of fire.\n--- Concussive Blasts\nWhen fired, these blobs travel in a straight line unaffected by gravity. Direct hits cause a knockdown.\n---- Level 1: Equipped with two Concussive Blasts.\n---- Level 2: Equipped with four Concussive Blasts\n---- Level 3: Equipped with six Concussive Blasts\n--- Ion Blasts\nIon Blasts deal electrical damage and stun enemies in a small area, preventing them from attacking while the effect lasts. Unlike Concussive Blasts, Ion Blasts are affected by gravity and travel in an arc. The closer the blast lands to an enemy, the longer the stun duration. They can also be charged to extend their range.\n---- Level 1: Equipped with two Ion Blasts.\n---- Level 2: Equipped with four Ion Blasts.\n---- Level 3: Equipped with six Ion Blasts.\n- \rClone Carbine\r\nThe DC-15 Carbine is a close to medium range alternative to the clone rifle, with an automatic The DC-15 Carbine is a close-to-medium range alternative to the Clone Rifle. It features a hard-hitting automatic primary fire, and a stun blast on secondary fire in place of blob launchers.\n-- Level 1: Unlocks the weapon with primary fire.\n-- Level 2: Unlocks stun blast, direct hit on enemies prevent them from attacking or jumping, and reduce their movement speed.\n-- Level 3: Increases clip size.\n> Abilities & Utility\n- Sprint ^3[Class Special 1]^7\n Enables the clone to run much faster, until their stamina reaches zero.\n- Reinforcements\n-- Level 1: Grants one additional life.\n- Stamina\nStamina fuels the Clone Trooper's Sprint ability ^3[CS1]^7, which dramatically boosts movement speed. Regeneration is fastest when walking or standing still.\n-- Level 1: Increases the regeneration speed of stamina.\n-- Level 2: Further increases regeneration. The Clone can continue sprinting while firing for double the stamina cost.\n-- Level 3: Even further increases the regeneration speed of stamina. Firing while sprinting has the normal stamina drain.\n"

REFERENCE           CLASSINFO_ARC
LANG_ENGLISH        "^1ARC TROOPER^7\nARCs are highly configurable spec-ops units generally oriented around speed, acrobatics, and versatile weaponry. They can also specialize in rocket artillery or droid-disabling pulse grenades.\n^2> Weaponry^7\n- \rClone Pistol\r\nThe primary fire on the clone pistol shoots a basic bolt. Holding secondary fire charges a shot that bounces off walls.\n-- Level 1: A standard-issue pistol, with nothing special about it.\n-- Level 2: Enables secondary charged bouncing shot - higher charge allows for more bounces.\n-- Level 3: Enables dual wield, double the fire power.\n- \rWestar M5\r\nAs versatile as the ARCs themselves, the M5 is a modular weapon configurable to mission requirements. It features a sniper mode for high-value targets and a pulse grenade launcher for suppressing or disabling enemy droids.\nIt also features a unique fixed-length clip reload. No matter how much ammo you're reloading, the reload will always take the same amount of time.\n-- Level 1: Grants the weapon with primary fire.\n-- Level 2: The gun is now always accurate.\n--- Scope\nAttaches a scope with a dedicated snipe mode. Combined with M5 Level 2 and Dexterity, this transforms the ARC into a highly mobile sniper.\n--- Grenade Launcher\nA pulse grenade launcher useful for clearing choke points or disabling enemy droids. Launched grenades travel at higher velocity than thrown grenades, but have a smaller area of effect and shorter stun duration\n---- Level 1: Grants the grenade launcher with a pulse grenade.\n---- Level 2: Grants another pulse grenade. Launched grenades will now stick to enemies and surfaces.\n- PLX-1\nA portable missile launcher with two projectile types: a standard Rocket and a Pulse Rocket. Pulse Rockets require Pulse Grenades and can be remotely detonated by tapping secondary fire before impact. The PLX-1 must be loaded after selection and switching away unloads it. Rockets explode if shot so be wary of enemy blaster fire.\n-- Level 1: Gives the PLX-1 launcher, and a single rocket.\n-- Level 2: Grants two more rockets.\n-- Level 3: Grants three more rockets, for a total of six.\n^3> Abilities & Utility^7\n- Sprint ^3[Class Special 1]^7\n Enables the ARC to sprint at greatly increased speed and perform acrobatics depending on Dexterity level, until stamina is depleted.\n- Dive ^3[Class Special 2]^7\nA forward roll which covers good distance, can be used to get to cover or dodge charging sith.\n- Dexterity\n-- Level 1: Allows the user to roll in any of four cardinal directions. Doing this roll forwards is an extremely useful tool for gaining long distance.\n-- Level 2: Allows the user to jump much higher than normal, perform flips in midair, and off of walls.\n-- Level 3: Grants the user limited protection from being knocked down, as long as one has stamina. When any force tries to knock you down that normally would (e.g. Force Push/Pull, an Explosion) the user will do a recovery roll and get up immediately. Also allows user to fire while knocked down or rolling. Additionally, users are able to do side wall flips and run on walls for a limited time.\n"

REFERENCE           CLASSINFO_WOOKIEE
LANG_ENGLISH        "^1WOOKIEE^7\nWookiees are the heavy gunners of the red team, built to absorb enemy fire and lay down overwhelming fire. They trade movement speed for exceptional durability and raw firepower.\n^2> Weaponry^7\n- \rPistol\r\nBasic pistol, always accurate with low firerate and modest damage.\n-- Level 1: A standard pistol.\n-- Level 2: Unlocks an alternate charged fire mode.\n- \rBowcaster\r\nA high-powered crossbow with solid fire rate, devastating damage, and large bolt size, excellent for clearing opponents at close range. A charge mode extends its effectiveness to long-range engagements.\n-- Level 1: Standard Bowcaster with high damage projectiles at a slow rate of fire.\n-- Level 2: Adds a scope and increases the rate of fire..\n-- Level 3: Enables Charged Firing mode (toggle with Weapon Mode Key) and increases the running accuracy of the Bowcaster significantly.\n- \rTraditional Bowcaster\r\nA very slow-firing weapon featuring a fan shot that splits into multiple bolts, devastating at close range, and a charged bolt capable of bouncing off walls and dealing massive damage.\n-- Level 1: Unlocks the primary fan shot, firing 3 bolts.\n-- Level 2: Fan shot now fires 5 bolts.\n-- Level 3: Grants a scope and secondary mode with charged bouncing shot.\n \n^3> Abilities & Utility^7\n- Wookiee Melee\nWookiee cannot be targeted by melee katas. In melee mode, alternate fire delivers a powerful slap that knocks down any non-crouching opponent (Droidekas excluded).\n- \rFrag Grenade\r\nA basic explosive grenade. Pressing and holding the primary fire key, while the grenade is selected will result in the grenade being charged. The longer the frag grenade is charged, the greater the throwing range capability becomes.\nAlternate fire of the grenade can be primed and with good timing made to explode right at the feet of the enemy, knocking them down instantly, the blast radius and damage done is vastly reduced in comparison to primary mode. Hitting an enemy directly will also detonate the grenade. Charging the alternate fire further extends the throwing range.\nSwitch to another weapon at any time to cancel a charge\n-- Level 1: One Frag Grenade.\n-- Level 2: Additional Frag Grenade.\n-- Level 3: Additional Frag Grenade.\n- Health\nThe Wookiee has the highest amount of health on the red team, it is crucial for this tanky class to stay alive, considering the Wookiee’s massive size.\n-- Level 1: Increases Wookiee’s health.\n-- Level 2: Further increases Wookiee’s health.\n-- Level 3: Even further increases Wookiee’s health.\n- Strength\nA slow Woookiee is a dead Wookiee. Strength keeps the Wookiee mobile and resilient, granting immunity to knockdowns and slows while boosting movement speed.\n-- Level 1: Increases melee damage per hit.\n-- Level 2: Further increases melee damage. The Wookiee becomes immune to knockdowns from Force Push/Pull, but can still be displaced by them. Movement speed in melee is increased.\n-- Level 3: Further increases melee damage. The Wookiee becomes immune to Force Grip, Force Lightning no longer prevents weapon fire. Most knockdown abilities and all displacements have no effect. Movement speed is further increased in melee and slightly improved with weapon drawn.\n- Fury\nGrants access to Wookiee Barge and activates the rage mechanic. Damaging enemies generates rage points, which fuel the Fury state. Melee attacks generate more rage. Exiting Fury leaves the Wookiee temporarily exhausted, reducing movement speed and melee damage for a short time.\n-- Level 1: Enables Wookiee Barge ^3[Class Special 2]^7, a forward charge that knocks down non-crouching enemies in Wookiee’s path. Enables Fury ^3[Class Special 1 in Melee]^7, Wookiee enters a state of fury, gaining movement speed, attack speed, and damage reduction. Rage points decay passively over time.\n-- Level 2: Boosts rage point generation. Slows the passive decay of rage points and reduces their drain while in Fury. Enhances Fury state with increased damage resistance.\n"

REFERENCE           CLASSINFO_DROIDEKA
LANG_ENGLISH        "^4DROIDEKA^7\nThe droideka is an ultra-hevy gunner and skirmisher/flanker. In deployed state it becomes capable of absorbing enormous amount of damage at the cost of severely limited manouverabilty. Packing up into roll mode makes the droideka very suspectible to damage but allows it to cover great distances very quickly.\n^2> Weaponry^7\nThe Droideka uses a built-in dual blaster, upgradeable with Firepower. Ammo regenerates passively over time.\n^3> Abilities & Utility^7\n- Shield Projector ^3[Class Special 1]^7\nThe Droideka's shield functions as a second health bar in deployed mode. It can be manually deactivated to regenerate. Lightsabers deal 2.5x damage to the shield and the Projectile Rifle can pierce it for 25% of its damage.\n-- Level 1: Shield only functions while stationary.\n-- Level 2: Shield now activates while deploying.\n-- Level 3: Shield functions while moving.\n- Shield Strength\n-- Level 1: Increases shield health.\n-- Level 2: Further increases shield healh.\n-- Level 3: Maximum shield health.\n- Hull Strength\n-- Level 1: Increases the Droideka’s health.\n-- Level 2: Further increases the Droideka’s healh.\n-- Level 3: The Deka no longer takes increased damage while rolling (from 1.5x to 1.0x).\n- Firepower\n-- Level 1: Increases ammo regeneration rate.\n-- Level 2: Increases the blaster fire rate.\n-- Level 3: Further increases both fire rate and ammo regeneration.\n- Advanced Logic\nProvides resistance against Jedi Mind Trick.\n-- Level 1: The SBD is able to see mind-tricking jedi flickering with a blue aura for a short period every 3 seconds.\n-- Level 2: The Jedi flickers once a second.\n- Shield Discharge ^3[Class Special 2]^7\nReleases a shockwave of concentrated shield energy that pushes all nearby enemies away. Airborne enemies caught in the blast are knocked down.\n-- Level 1: Enables Shield Discharge.\n- Quick Deploy\n-- Level 1: Speeds up the deployment animation.\n-- Level 2: Speeds up the pack-up animation.\n- Power Management\nEnables the transfer of power between the shield and ammo systems using alternate fire. Press the weapon mode key to swap between Shield-to-Ammo mode and Ammo-to-Shield mode.\n-- Level 1: Enables power management.\n"

REFERENCE           CLASSINFO_BH
LANG_ENGLISH        "^4BOUNTY HUNTER^7\nA marksman and skirmisher class specializing in long-range combat. Armed with two powerful sniper rifle options capable of eliminating targets in a single shot, combined with exceptional movement speed, the Bounty Hunter is a threat to every Rebel class.\n\n^2> Weaponry\n- \rPistol\r\n^7With low firerate, high damage and full accuracy the pistol is a high skill ceiling option capable of quickly dispatching enemies.\n-- Level 1: A standard pistol.\n-- Level 2: Unlocks an alternate charged fire mode.\n-- Level 3: Grants a high-powered primary fire and charge mode with increased ammo consumption. Toggle weapon mode to revert to the standard pistol.\n\n- \rE-11 Blaster\r\n^7The E-11 is a very versatile blaster rifle featuring two firing modes, a slow firing primary fire, which deals higher damage and is of higher velocity, and secondary fire for close range engagements.\n-- Level 1: A standard blaster rifle with slow primary fire and high velocity.\n-- Level 2: Adds a faster firing alt. fire.\n-- Level 3: Makes alt.fire accurate when walking and standing still, and increases the clip capacity.\n\n- \rDLT-20a\r\n^7A slow-firing rifle with modest damage on its own, the DLT-20a becomes a powerhouse through its burst fire mode\n-- Level 1: A medium-powered high-velocity rifle.\n-- Level 2: Adds a burst mode (toggle with Weapon Mode key).\n-- Level 3: Adds a scope on the alt. fire button.\n\n- \rProjectile Rifle\r\nA dedicated sniper weapon that cannot be upgraded. Features two zoom levels switched with weapon mode. Must always be fired while scoped, jumping while scoped is not possible, and the rifle is only accurate when standing completely still.\n\n- \rDisruptor\r\nA slow-firing hitscan weapon with perfect accuracy at all times. When scoped, it transforms into a charged sniper capable of tearing through targets.\n-- Level 1: Unscoped hit-scan shot and a scope.\n-- Level 2: Allows a charged shot whilst scoped. Can shoot through multiple targets.\n\n^3> Abilities & Utility^7 \n- Advanced Melee\nBounty hunter can use melee moves with their weapon drawn. Use Class Special 1 combined with a movement key to perform a kick, CS1 + Crouch to perform a sweep kick, or Forward + Use + CS1 to air-kick. Use these moves to catch a Jedi off-guard and knock them down when they get close.\n\n- \rThermal Detonator\r\nA grenade which disintegrates anything within its blast radius.\n\n- \rPoison Dart\r ^3[Class Special 1 in Melee]^7\nPoison darts do a small amount of damage every second over a period of time. They also slow down Force pool regeneration. 1 dart available per level (max. 3).\n\n- \rTracking Dart\r ^3[Class Special 2 in Melee]^7\nTracker darts allow you to track one or more targets through walls etc. Tracked targets will periodically flash with the color depending on their health level (green – healthy, red – heavily wounded). Comes in packs of 2 (max. 6 darts)."

ENDMARKER
